course: dictionary
lesson: 3702
title: What is a flatworm?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A flatworm is a simple, soft worm. Its body is flat, like a ribbon, and it has no legs. Many flatworms live in water or in damp places, such as under stones or logs.
explain: Flatworms are among the simplest animals that have a head and a tail. That makes them a useful first step when scientists study how animals are built.
explain: Some flatworms are parasites. A parasite lives in or on another animal and gets its food from it. Tapeworms are flatworms that live in the guts of animals.
explain: Read this: «Some flatworms can regrow from pieces.» It means a flatworm cut into bits may grow new parts. Planarian flatworms can even regrow a lost head or tail.
fact: A flatworm is a simple, soft worm with a flat body and no legs.
fact: Many flatworms live in water or in damp places.
fact: A parasite is an animal that lives in or on another animal and feeds on it.
fact: «Planarian flatworms» can regrow lost parts of their body.
fact: Garden flatworms can harm earthworms in New Zealand and the UK.
exercise: What kind of body does a flatworm have? | *A flat body with no legs | A round body with six legs | A hard shell with a long neck
exercise: «Some flatworms can regrow from pieces.» What does regrow mean? | *To grow again after being lost or cut | To lay eggs in the mud | To swim very fast | To shrink away to nothing
exercise: What is a parasite? | *An animal that lives in or on another animal and feeds on it | An animal with no head or tail | A worm that only lives in the sea | A plant that grows in the dark
test: Where do many flatworms live? | *In water or damp places | Inside rocks of ice | In the desert sand | On the moon
test: Why are some pets given worming tablets? | Because worms make pets sleepy | Because pets need to grow taller | *Because tapeworms, a kind of flatworm, can live in their guts
exam: Which sentence is true? | Flatworms can never live in water | A flatworm has legs and a round body | Flatworms are the largest animals on Earth | *A flatworm is a simple soft worm with a flat body and no legs
